  "notes": "ETYMOLOGY:\n{詰|つ}め (packing, filling) + {替|か}え (replacement) - from {詰|つ}める (to pack) + {替|か}える (to replace)\n\nECO-FRIENDLY SHOPPING:\n{詰|つ}め{替|か}え products are popular in Japan for reducing plastic waste. They come in pouches (パウチ) that are transferred into reusable bottles.\n\nCOMMON PRODUCTS:\n- シャンプー{詰|つ}め{替|か}え - shampoo refill\n- {洗剤|せんざい}{詰|つ}め{替|か}え - detergent refill\n- ハンドソープ{詰|つ}め{替|か}え - hand soap refill\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {詰|つ}め{替|か}え{用|よう} - refill type/for refilling\n- {詰|つ}め{替|か}えパック - refill pack",
